  "notes": "Berlin's styles (de-berlin) on europe-west: Gründerzeit Altbau fronts and their courtyard wings, post-war infill, Plattenbau, Karl-Marx-Allee's tiles, the Hansaviertel's slabs, Neubau stone, post-war concrete, Prussian sandstone, red and yellow brick, churches. Their wall detail (fade bays: only where the bays are resolved, Berlin M4) is the core features' and the patterns' (facade/core.js): Gründerzeit stucco (surrounds, hoods, pediments, profiled cornice, string courses), rustication, French balconies, pilasters, frieze, ceramic tiles, Plattenbau, slab edges, stone joints, precast joints, brick courses, sill bands, buttresses, shopfronts with letters. Inherited from europe-west and kept as they are until stage 3 decides: house's shutters, brickstone's floor bands, surrounds and quoins, concretepanel's panel spandrels and limestone's guard rails (Paris's features: built into Berlin's shader for these rows); brickstone, concretepanel and house lit as homes.",
